{
    "background_story": "Rose was a shy and introverted young artist who worked as a florist in a small shop. One day, a renowned sculptor, Henry, stumbled upon her store and was struck by her beauty and potential. Inspired by the myth of Pygmalion, Henry saw an opportunity to mold Rose into a masterpiece. He began to mentor her, teaching her about art, literature, and the world beyond her humble shop. As Rose's confidence grew, so did her talents. Henry's guidance and encouragement transformed her into a refined and elegant woman, much like the statue of Galatea from the myth. Together, they created breathtaking works of art, with Rose's beauty and creativity shining through. Their collaboration sparked a romance, and Rose became the muse and love of Henry's life, proving that with the right guidance, anyone can be transformed into a work of art.",
